WEBVTT

1
00:00:25.583 --> 00:00:29.833


2
00:00:29.833 --> 00:00:32.666
<b>In previous verses, Krishna explained</b>

3
00:00:32.666 --> 00:00:37.208
<b>that a wise person should </b>
<b>not criticize or restrict others,</b>

4
00:00:37.208 --> 00:00:40.583
<b>they should become an example </b>
<b>of excellence themselves,</b>

5
00:00:40.583 --> 00:00:46.041
<b>but rather inspire them to follow the </b>
<b>path of true knowledge.</b>

6
00:00:46.041 --> 00:00:50.458
<b>Now in this verse, Krishna speaks about</b>
<b>the ignorant person</b>

7
00:00:50.458 --> 00:00:54.583
<b>and their way of thinking.</b>

8
00:00:58.875 --> 00:01:04.291
<b>Krishna explains that one who lacks </b>
<b>spiritual knowledge and lives in delusion –</b>

9
00:01:04.291 --> 00:01:09.666
<b>such an ignorant person considers themselves </b>
<b>the sole controller of all their actions.</b>

10
00:01:09.666 --> 00:01:12.625
<b>They are consumed by the ego of 'I',</b>

11
00:01:12.625 --> 00:01:18.250
<b>constantly thinking that everything </b>
<b>happening is their doing:</b>

12
00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:20.208
<b>"I achieved success,"</b>

13
00:01:20.208 --> 00:01:21.625
<b>"I am doing this,</b>

14
00:01:21.625 --> 00:01:23.375
<b>"I am doing that."</b>

15
00:01:23.375 --> 00:01:29.083
<b>When any action yields good results, </b>
<b>they take complete credit for it,</b>

16
00:01:29.083 --> 00:01:32.250
<b>which only inflates their ego further.</b>

17
00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:36.708
<b>And when results are unfavorable, </b>
<b>their mind turns bitter –</b>

18
00:01:36.708 --> 00:01:44.000
<b>they either blame others and circumstances, </b>
<b>or begin to curse themselves.</b>

19
00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.416
<b>Even in this self-criticism, ego lurks beneath,</b>

20
00:01:46.416 --> 00:01:48.750
<b>as they believe,</b>

21
00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:52.375
<b>they could have completely </b>
<b>controlled the circumstances,</b>

22
00:01:52.375 --> 00:01:57.458
<b>other people, and themselves </b>
<b>if they had wanted to. </b>

23
00:01:57.458 --> 00:01:59.125
<b>Whether good or bad,</b>

24
00:01:59.125 --> 00:02:02.500
<b>every outcome affects and disturbs them.</b>

25
00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:09.041
<b>The truth is that they are unaware </b>
<b>that human actions and conduct</b>

26
00:02:09.041 --> 00:02:13.166
<b>are bound by the three qualities of nature - </b>
<b>Tamas, Rajas, and Sattva.</b>

27
00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:16.958
<b>Where Tamas represents lethargy and ignorance,</b>

28
00:02:16.958 --> 00:02:20.041
<b>Rajas symbolizes desires and struggle,</b>

29
00:02:20.041 --> 00:02:24.833
<b>and Sattva represents peace and harmony.</b>

30
00:02:24.833 --> 00:02:28.250
<b>These three qualities exist in varying </b>
<b>proportions in every human being,</b>

31
00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:31.166
<b>and they determine one's actions.</b>

32
00:02:31.166 --> 00:02:34.000
<b>The ignorant person, unaware of this truth,</b>

33
00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:38.083
<b>instead of acquiring knowledge to </b>
<b>transform the influence of these qualities</b>

34
00:02:38.083 --> 00:02:46.166
<b>and advance spiritually, merely keeps </b>
<b>trying to change their actions and results.</b>

35
00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:50.458
<b>Moreover, such an ignorant person</b>
<b> is never grateful.</b>

36
00:02:50.458 --> 00:02:56.083
<b>They overlook many factors that assist them.</b>

37
00:02:56.083 --> 00:03:04.875
<b>It's like a student who takes complete </b>
<b>credit for good exam results,</b>

38
00:03:04.875 --> 00:03:11.208
<b>forgetting to acknowledge their parents </b>
<b>who enrolled them in a good school,</b>

39
00:03:11.208 --> 00:03:18.625
<b>the teachers who educated them, </b>
<b>and the classmates who helped them.</b>

40
00:03:18.625 --> 00:03:26.208
<b>One who gives credit only to themselves </b>
<b>is truly deluded – the greatest of fools.</b>

41
00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.708
<b>Whether passing an exam,</b>

42
00:03:33.708 --> 00:03:35.375
<b>winning a game,</b>

43
00:03:35.375 --> 00:03:38.125
<b>or achieving professional success...</b>

44
00:03:38.125 --> 00:03:41.291
<b>often in life, we assume</b>

45
00:03:41.291 --> 00:03:49.750
<b>that our achievements are </b>
<b>solely the result of our own efforts.</b>

46
00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:52.458
<b>However, we must recognize</b>

47
00:03:52.458 --> 00:04:00.083
<b>that numerous factors and </b>
<b>aspects contribute to our success.</b>

48
00:04:00.083 --> 00:04:03.791
<b>And the same applies to failure.</b>

49
00:04:03.791 --> 00:04:11.166
<b>Consider a student who </b>
<b>scores excellently in an exam.</b>

50
00:04:11.166 --> 00:04:21.166
<b>They might think it's purely due to </b>
<b>their efforts and intelligence.</b>

51
00:04:21.166 --> 00:04:22.250
<b>But</b>

52
00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:24.208
<b>is this the whole truth?</b>

53
00:04:24.208 --> 00:04:26.083
<b>No.</b>

54
00:04:26.083 --> 00:04:29.958
<b>Many elements contributed to their success:</b>

55
00:04:29.958 --> 00:04:35.708
<b>parents who enrolled them in a good school,</b>

56
00:04:35.708 --> 00:04:39.791
<b>teachers who educated them,</b>

57
00:04:39.791 --> 00:04:45.000
<b>and even circumstances played a role.</b>

58
00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:51.875
<b>Perhaps the exam focused on </b>
<b>subjects where the student excelled.</b>

59
00:04:51.875 --> 00:04:56.250
<b>When you remain grateful to </b>
<b>others and circumstances,</b>

60
00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:59.875
<b>success won't breed ego.</b>

61
00:04:59.875 --> 00:05:07.083
<b>This mindset shifts you away from pride and </b>
<b>towards humility and gratitude.</b>

62
00:05:07.083 --> 00:05:12.041
<b>This perspective also helps during failure.</b>

63
00:05:12.041 --> 00:05:12.916
<b>Because,</b>

64
00:05:12.916 --> 00:05:17.166
<b>if outcomes don't depend entirely on you,</b>

65
00:05:17.166 --> 00:05:22.083
<b>then failure isn't entirely your fault either.</b>

66
00:05:22.083 --> 00:05:29.083
<b>Instead of self-criticism, you learn </b>
<b>to take lessons from failure</b>

67
00:05:29.083 --> 00:05:34.333
<b>and focus on improving your approach.</b>

68
00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:36.833
<b>This is what the Gita teaches –</b>

69
00:05:36.833 --> 00:05:41.041
<b>only your efforts are in your hands,</b>

70
00:05:41.041 --> 00:05:42.916
<b>not the results.</b>

71
00:05:42.916 --> 00:05:44.125
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

72
00:05:44.125 --> 00:05:50.291
<b>This mindset will help you </b>
<b>in every situation, good or bad.</b>

73
00:05:54.958 --> 00:05:59.166
<b>Ego.</b>

74
00:05:59.166 --> 00:06:03.958
<b>The ego of attributing every </b>
<b>achievement solely to oneself</b>

75
00:06:03.958 --> 00:06:09.708
<b>harms even familial relationships </b>
<b>and their sweetness.</b>

76
00:06:09.708 --> 00:06:12.250
<b>For example,</b>

77
00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:16.500
<b>if, in the excitement of your </b>
<b>achievements, in your ego,</b>

78
00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:19.375
<b>you keep saying in front of everyone</b>

79
00:06:19.375 --> 00:06:22.875
<b>that this is the fruit of your efforts,</b>

80
00:06:22.875 --> 00:06:25.541
<b>how inappropriate would that be?</b>

81
00:06:25.541 --> 00:06:27.708
<b>What about the better half</b>

82
00:06:27.708 --> 00:06:31.875
<b>who managed the entire household so that</b>
<b>its burden does not fall on you?</b>

83
00:06:31.875 --> 00:06:36.916
<b>What about the children whose share </b>
<b>of time you gave to your work?</b>

84
00:06:36.916 --> 00:06:45.250
<b>Such behavior is not only inappropriate</b>
<b>but also neglectful of the family.</b>

85
00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:47.833
<b>And where there is neglect,</b>

86
00:06:47.833 --> 00:06:53.500
<b>the sweetness of relationships</b>
<b>will slowly fade away.</b>

87
00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:55.583
<b>Unfortunately,</b>

88
00:06:55.583 --> 00:07:00.375
<b>many times a person understands</b>
<b>this when it is too late,</b>

89
00:07:00.375 --> 00:07:04.166
<b>when he has become emotionally alone,</b>

90
00:07:04.166 --> 00:07:07.541
<b>and then it is known that</b>

91
00:07:07.541 --> 00:07:12.541
<b>the true joy of success lies only </b>
<b>in sharing it with family.</b>

92
00:07:12.541 --> 00:07:15.166
<b>Not just family,</b>

93
00:07:15.166 --> 00:07:22.291
<b>you must be grateful for the contributions </b>
<b>of all those who helped in any way –</b>

94
00:07:22.291 --> 00:07:26.250
<b>those friends who suggested</b>
<b>a way out during dilemmas,</b>

95
00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:31.041
<b>those well-wishers who told you about </b>
<b>a beneficial opportunity,</b>

96
00:07:31.041 --> 00:07:33.208
<b>and many other such people.</b>

97
00:07:33.208 --> 00:07:35.375
<b>If you don't do this,</b>

98
00:07:35.375 --> 00:07:38.291
<b>if you remain absorbed only in yourself,</b>

99
00:07:38.291 --> 00:07:46.583
<b>a day will come when there will be </b>
<b>no one with you to share the joy of this success.</b>

100
00:07:46.583 --> 00:07:47.875
<b>Also, </b>

101
00:07:47.875 --> 00:07:55.250
<b>if ever failure comes, then there will be</b>
<b>no shoulder to express grief.</b>

102
00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:59.458
<b>Ego in relationships is like poison;</b>

103
00:07:59.458 --> 00:08:00.833
<b>beware of it.</b>

104
00:08:00.833 --> 00:08:04.708
<b>Gratitude, on the other hand, is nectar;</b>

105
00:08:04.708 --> 00:08:07.416
<b>consume it.</b>

106
00:08:07.416 --> 00:08:09.041
<b>Contemplate.</b>

107
00:08:13.708 --> 00:08:16.208
<b>In any professional organization,</b>

108
00:08:16.208 --> 00:08:21.416
<b>the nature and conduct of the senior </b>
<b>officials appointed to leadership positions</b>

109
00:08:21.416 --> 00:08:28.333
<b>slowly become the nature of the organization </b>
<b>and the nature of the people working there.</b>

110
00:08:28.333 --> 00:08:30.541
<b>Imagine</b>

111
00:08:30.541 --> 00:08:31.833
<b>what would happen</b>

112
00:08:31.833 --> 00:08:37.250
<b>if a senior official attributes the </b>
<b>credit for every success only to himself,</b>

113
00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:39.625
<b>not sharing it with anyone.</b>

114
00:08:39.625 --> 00:08:41.208
<b>First of all,</b>

115
00:08:41.208 --> 00:08:48.416
<b>in such an environment, will the people working </b>
<b>there be willing to give their full contribution?</b>

116
00:08:48.416 --> 00:08:49.916
<b>No.</b>

117
00:08:49.916 --> 00:08:55.958
<b>Also, this same trait will slowly spread </b>
<b>to other people as well.</b>

118
00:08:55.958 --> 00:08:59.208
<b>Everyone will get into the race to grab credit.</b>

119
00:08:59.208 --> 00:09:02.250
<b>Mutual cooperation will begin to break.</b>

120
00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:06.333
<b>In such a situation, if someone has </b>
<b>a good suggestion,</b>

121
00:09:06.333 --> 00:09:13.458
<b>he will keep it hidden out of the </b>
<b>worry that someone else might take credit for it.</b>

122
00:09:13.458 --> 00:09:16.625
<b>That person will give suggestions</b>

123
00:09:16.625 --> 00:09:20.791
<b>only when he has full assurance </b>
<b>of getting credit for it.</b>

124
00:09:20.791 --> 00:09:24.000
<b>Unfortunately,</b>

125
00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:28.291
<b>such changes in the nature of </b>
<b>employees are not directly visible</b>

126
00:09:28.291 --> 00:09:34.916
<b>but internally, like termites, they begin</b>
<b>to hollow out that organization.</b>

127
00:09:34.916 --> 00:09:36.000
<b>Also,</b>

128
00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:41.208
<b>those who want to work with honesty, </b>
<b>who want to progress,</b>

129
00:09:41.208 --> 00:09:48.500
<b>find such an environment corrupt, </b>
<b>and they start looking for other options.</b>

130
00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:50.125
<b>Slowly,</b>

131
00:09:50.125 --> 00:09:54.750
<b>only competition remains in </b>
<b>the organization instead of cooperation.</b>

132
00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:58.458
<b>In which the employees there may win or lose,</b>

133
00:09:58.458 --> 00:10:00.291
<b>but</b>

134
00:10:00.291 --> 00:10:03.750
<b>the organization definitely loses.</b>

135
00:10:03.750 --> 00:10:05.333
<b>Credit.</b>

136
00:10:05.333 --> 00:10:09.916
<b>This word is small but extremely powerful.</b>

137
00:10:09.916 --> 00:10:14.625
<b>If it is taken with selfishness, </b>
<b>not shared with others,</b>

138
00:10:14.625 --> 00:10:17.750
<b>then it will become poison for the organization.</b>

139
00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:22.375
<b>The same credit, if shared with everyone,</b>

140
00:10:22.375 --> 00:10:26.583
<b>will run as a power in that organization.</b>

141
00:10:26.583 --> 00:10:29.041
<b>Sharing credit with others in success</b>

142
00:10:29.041 --> 00:10:32.666
<b>and taking responsibility on oneself in failure</b>

143
00:10:32.666 --> 00:10:35.708
<b>is the key to strong leadership.</b>

144
00:10:35.708 --> 00:10:37.291
<b>Contemplate.</b>

